        "notes": "Constant motor torque on the left finger (torque-driven, forward dynamics), gravity off, start at rest. The initial angular acceleration is torque / (I_left + ratio^2 I_right) about the pivots. Ideal transmission: q_right = ratio x q_left (ratio -1: mirror motion). The coupling is massless, rigid, lossless, without backlash and without friction; the right finger is driven by the constraint, not by a second motor. The motor effort reported on the left joint includes the effort that the constraint transmits to the right finger.",
        "print_settings": {},
        "mbd": {
