        "notes": "Prescribed hold at the closing angle (velocity zero) with an explicit outward force on each fingertip, as if squeezing an object (no contact model). The loads are in the finger frame, perpendicular to the finger, so the lever arm is the finger length. Gravity off. The joint reactions are the load for a structural static-hold study. Ideal transmission: q_right = ratio x q_left (ratio -1: mirror motion). The coupling is massless, rigid, lossless, without backlash and without friction; the right finger is driven by the constraint, not by a second motor. The motor effort reported on the left joint includes the effort that the constraint transmits to the right finger.",
